======================================================================
CATEGORY 1: 1/e IN OPTIMIZATION THEORY
======================================================================

H-EXT-01: Optimal LR for SGD on f(x)=0.5*x^2
  Claim: optimal constant LR for 1-step convergence = 1/e
  Theory: For f(x)=0.5*a*x^2, optimal LR=1/a (not 1/e).
  But for NOISY quadratic with Gaussian noise sigma=1,
  what LR minimizes E[f(x_T)] after T steps?
  Best LR = 0.0200, 1/e = 0.3679
  Error vs 1/e: 94.6%
  Grade: ⚪  (best_lr=0.0200; likely 1/a regime, not 1/e)

H-EXT-02: Optimal simulated annealing cooling factor
  Claim: optimal T_new/T_old ratio per step ~ 1-1/e or 1/e?
  Best cooling = 0.9000
  1 - 1/e = 0.6321,  1/e = 0.3679
  Grade: ⚪  (cool=0.9000, 1-cool=0.1000)

H-EXT-03: Optimal epsilon-greedy exploration rate = 1/e?
  Known: secretary problem optimal threshold = 1/e
  Test: multi-armed bandit epsilon-greedy
  Best epsilon = 0.1100, 1/e = 0.3679
  Grade: ⚪  (eps=0.1100 (closer to ln(4/3)))

H-EXT-04: Optimal SGD momentum ~ 1-1/e?
  Claim: 1-1/e = 0.6321...
  Best momentum = 0.0000, 1-1/e = 0.6321
  Grade: ⚪  (mom=0.0000)

======================================================================
CATEGORY 2: 1/e IN INFORMATION THEORY
======================================================================

H-EXT-05: Binary source rate-distortion inflection at D=1/e?
  R(D) = 1 - H(D) for D in [0, 0.5], H = binary entropy
  Inflection = where R''(D) = 0, i.e. H''(D) = 0
  Max curvature at D = 0.4989, 1/e = 0.3679
  Grade: ⚪  (maxcurv_D=0.4989)

H-EXT-06: Optimal compression ratio for random source ~ 1/e?
  Shannon: random binary with p(1)=p has entropy H(p).
  Minimum description = H(p) bits/symbol.
  Ratio = H(p)/1 = H(p). At what p is ratio = 1/e?
  H(p)=1/e at p = 0.070525
  Grade: ⚪  (p=0.0705, closest to GZ_LOWER)

H-EXT-07: Z-channel capacity at crossover probability p=1/e
  Z-channel: 0->0 always, 1->0 with prob p, 1->1 with prob 1-p
  C(1/e) = 0.436401 bits
  Grade: ⚪  (C=0.4364, closest to 1/2 (err=12.7%))

======================================================================
CATEGORY 3: ln(4/3) IN NUMBER THEORY
======================================================================

H-EXT-08: ln(4/3) from alternating harmonic series
  ln(2) = sum_{n=1}^inf (-1)^(n+1)/n
  ln(4/3) = 2*ln(2) - ln(3) ... check partial sums
  ln(1+1/3) converges at n=22 terms
  Alt harmonic S_N never comes within 0.001 of ln(4/3)
  EXACT: ln(4/3) = sum_{n=1}^inf (-1)^(n+1)/(n*3^n)
  This is ln(1+1/3) Taylor series — KNOWN identity
  Grade: 🟩  (ln(4/3)=ln(1+1/3)=sum(-1)^(n+1)/(n*3^n), exact)

H-EXT-09: ln(4/3) relationship to Mertens constant M
  Mertens: M = lim(sum 1/p - ln(ln(n))) = 0.2615...
  ln(4/3) = 0.287682
  Mertens = 0.261497
  Diff    = 0.026185
  Ratio   = 1.100134
  Grade: 🟧★  (ratio=1.1001, diff=0.0262)

H-EXT-10: ln(4/3) continued fraction pattern
  CF = [0, 3, 2, 9, 1, 16, 2, 2, 4, 1, 4, 5, 1, 2, 3]
  CF(1/e) = [0, 2, 1, 2, 1, 1, 4, 1, 1, 6, 1, 1, 8, 1, 1]
  Sum of CF[1:7] = 33
  Grade: ⚪  (CF=[0,3,2,9,1,16,2,2,4,1,4,5...], not periodic (transcendental))

