CATEGORY 4: n=6 IN GRAPH THEORY
======================================================================

H-EXT-11: K(3,3) chromatic number and n=6
  K(3,3) is complete bipartite: 6 vertices, 9 edges
  chi(K(3,3)) = 2 (bipartite => 2-colorable)
  Edge chromatic (chromatic index) chi'(K(3,3)) = 3
  Key fact: K(3,3) is the smallest non-planar graph (Kuratowski)
  chi * chi' = 2 * 3 = 6 = |V(K(3,3))| = 6
  Grade: 🟩  (chi(K33)*chi'(K33)=2*3=6=|V|, exact)

H-EXT-12: R(3,3) = 6. R(3,3)/e and other combinations
