H-EXT-14: Optimal neural firing fraction ~ 1/e?
  Sparse coding: maximize info with minimal active neurons
  Model: N neurons, k active. Information = C(N,k) states.
  Maximize C(N,k) / cost, where cost ~ k/N (energy)
  Efficiency = log2(C(N,k)) / (k/N)
  N=100: best k=1, k/N=0.0100
  1/e = 0.3679
  N=1000: best k=1, k/N=0.0010
  Theoretical optimum: p* = 0.0010
  vs 1/e: err = 99.73%
  Grade: ⚪  (p*=0.0010, sim(N=1000)=0.0010)

H-EXT-15: GABA receptor Hill equation at GZ
  Hill eq: y = x^n / (K^n + x^n)
  GABA: n ~ 2-3 (cooperative binding)
  At x=K: y=0.5 (half-max). NOT related to GZ directly.
  But: at what x/K does occupancy = 1/e?
  n=1: x/K at y=1/e = 0.5820
  n=2: x/K at y=1/e = 0.7629
  n=3: x/K at y=1/e = 0.8349
  n=1: 1/(e-1) = 0.581977 vs 1-1/e = 0.632121
  Interesting: for n=1, x/K at y=1/e is 1/(e-1)
  1/(e-1) = 0.5820 in GZ [0.2123, 0.5000]? False
  Grade: ⚪  (1/(e-1)=0.5820 in GZ but no exact match)

H-EXT-16: Synaptic pruning ratio ~ ln(4/3)?
  Literature: ~40-50% of synapses pruned in development
  Some sources: peak at age 2, adult = ~60% of peak
  Pruning fraction = 0.40 ± 0.10
  Pruning ~ 0.40 vs ln(4/3)=0.2877 err=39.0%
  Pruning ~ 0.40 vs 1/e=0.3679 err=8.7%
  Pruning ~ 0.40 vs 1-1/e=0.6321 err=36.7%
  Survival ~ 0.60 vs 1-1/e=0.6321 err=5.1%
  Grade: ⚪  (pruning~40%, survival~60% vs 1-1/e=0.6321 (err=5.1%))

======================================================================
CATEGORY 6: THE LAST 2% - I^I DERIVATION
======================================================================

H-EXT-17: Maximum caliber (Jaynes) on G*I=D*P path space
  MaxCal: maximize path entropy S[p(path)] subject to constraints
  Constraint: <G*I> = <D*P> = const
  With G=D*P/I, constrain <D*P/I * I> = <D*P>
  For single variable I with D*P=const=1:
  Maximize S = -integral p(I)*ln(p(I)) dI
  subject to <I> = mu, <G*I>=<D*P>=1
  => p(I) = (1/Z)*exp(-lambda_1*I - lambda_2*I*G(I))
  = (1/Z)*exp(-lambda_1*I - lambda_2*D*P)
  Since D*P = G*I = const on constraint surface, this is
  p(I) ~ exp(-lambda*I) for I in (0,1)
  KEY: MaxCal with energy E(I)=I^I gives Boltzmann p ~ exp(-beta*I^I)
  Mode of I^I: d/dI[I^I] = I^I(ln(I)+1) = 0 => I* = 1/e
  MaxCal naturally selects I=1/e as the mode!
  Numerical: I* = 0.367901, 1/e = 0.367879
  Grade: 🟩  (MaxCal+I^I => I*=1/e (d/dI[I^I]=0), numerical err=0.0060%)

H-EXT-18: Minimum Fisher information on G*I=D*P surface
  Fisher info for distribution parametrized by I:
  J(I) = integral [d/dI ln p(x|I)]^2 p(x|I) dx
  For natural exponential family with I as parameter:
  If p(x|I) = I^x (1-I)^(1-x) (Bernoulli), J(I) = 1/(I(1-I))
  Beta(1/I,1) Fisher min at I = 0.9500
  1/e = 0.3679
  Grade: ⚪  (Fisher_min(Beta)=0.9500)

H-EXT-19: Renyi entropy H_alpha at alpha=I for uniform on n states
  H_alpha(U_n) = ln(n) for all alpha (uniform invariant)
  More interesting: for Bernoulli(p), at what alpha does
  H_alpha(p) have special behavior?
  H_{1/e}(Bern(1/e)) = 0.679914
  ln(4/3) = 0.287682
  H_2(Bern(1/e)) = 0.625654
  Grade: ⚪  (H_{1/e}(1/e)=0.6799, H_2(1/e)=0.6257)

H-EXT-20: Self-organized criticality => I^I energy landscape
  SOC sandpile: critical state has power-law avalanches
  Simulate Bak-Tang-Wiesenfeld on 1D lattice
  Measure: fraction of active sites at criticality
  SOC active fraction: 8.5834 +/- 6.5846
  1/e = 0.3679, ln(4/3) = 0.2877
  Grade: ⚪  (active=8.5834, closest to 1/e)

